# pds/pds-healthping.timer — the schedule for pds-healthping.service.
#
# Every five minutes. The external dead-man's switch's own grace period should
# be set to a small multiple of this (fifteen minutes is a reasonable pairing),
# so one missed ping from a momentary blip does not page, but a real outage
# does within a quarter of an hour.
#
# Persistent= is deliberately ABSENT — the opposite of pds-backup.timer. A
# missed backup should run late, because the point is to have an archive. A
# missed liveness ping must NEVER be replayed later: a ping sent at boot for a
# window the box spent switched off would report health for exactly the outage
# the switch exists to detect. That is the [W-QUIETER] shape and it would make
# this mechanism worse than not having it.

[Unit]
Description=Five-minute health-gated dead-man's-switch ping
Requires=pds-healthping.service

[Timer]
OnBootSec=2min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min
AccuracySec=30s

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
